course: dictionary
lesson: 12257
title: Contaminant: the unwanted, harmful extra
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A contaminant is something unwanted that gets into something else and makes it dirty, impure or harmful. Look at the word parts in the sentence to find clues. «The river water had a contaminant in it, so the sign said Do not drink.» The sign warns you, so the contaminant must be something that makes the water unsafe.
explain: Contaminants can be tiny things you cannot see, such as germs, or substances such as oil, lead or plastic. «Oil on the beach is a contaminant that harms the sea birds.» The harm to the birds tells you the oil is bad news. Always ask: is this thing clean and safe, or is it spoiling something?
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you put «something harmful that spoils the water» in place of contaminant and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Context clues like warnings, harm and danger often point to a contaminant.
fact: A contaminant is a substance that makes something dirty, impure, harmful or poisonous.
fact: Contaminants can be germs, chemicals, dirt or plastics.
fact: Contaminants can get into water, food, air and soil.
fact: «Contaminant» is a noun, so you can have one contaminant or many contaminants.
fact: Water companies test for contaminants to keep tap water safe.
exercise: «The river water had a contaminant in it, so the sign said Do not drink.» What is a contaminant? | *Something that makes water dirty or harmful | A sign that tells boats where to go | A kind of fish that lives in rivers | Something that makes water warm
exercise: «Oil on the beach is a contaminant that harms the sea birds.» Why is oil called a contaminant? | Because it makes the beach bigger | *Because it makes the sea and beach dirty and harmful | Because it is clean and makes the sand shine | Because it is a kind of bird
exercise: «Lead is a dangerous contaminant found in some old pipes.» Find and copy one word that means harmful. | *dangerous | pipes | contaminant | found
test: Water companies test for «contaminants» in tap water. Why do they do this? | To stop people from washing their hands | To make the water taste of sweets | *To keep the tap water safe to drink | To find out how deep the water is
test: The food was spoiled by a ___ from dirty hands. Which word fits best? | contents | continent | contest | *contaminant
exam: Mia says a contaminant is something clean and safe. Is she right? | No, it means a kind of board game | Yes, it means a bright, sunny day | Yes, it means something clean and safe | *No, it is something dirty, impure or harmful
